  "result": "Perfect! All 72 tests pass. I've successfully added line discounts:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **New error code in `src/errors.js`:**\n   - `DISCOUNT_INVALID` \u2014 for discount values outside 0-100 or non-numeric\n\n2. **New functions in `src/invoices.js`:**\n   - **`lineDiscount(line)`** \u2014 Calculates discount as lineTotal \u00d7 (discountPercent / 100), rounded and clamped to 0\n   - **`validateDiscount(discountPercent)`** \u2014 Internal validator for discount values\n\n3. **Updated existing functions:**\n   - **`invoiceTotals()`** \u2014 Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where total = subtotal - discount, all clamped to 0\n   - **`createInvoice()`** \u2014 Accepts optional `discountPercent` (0-100, can have decimals) in line input, validates it\n   - **`addLine()`** \u2014 Accepts optional `discountPercent` in input, validates it\n\n4. **Tests added (15 new discount-related tests):**\n   - lineDiscount calculations with integers and decimals\n   - Default discount (0) when omitted\n   - createInvoice accepting/validating discounts\n   - invoiceTotals calculating subtotal, discount, and total\n   - addLine accepting/validating discounts\n   - Amount clamping to 0 minimum\n   - Render tests for discounted totals\n\nAll calculations use `roundCents()` for proper rounding, and amounts are always clamped to 0 minimum as per requirements.",
